sentences.l:
Already you yourself, I think, looking on,
know that a woe a god is rolling on the Danaans,
and the victory is the Trojans’;

But you, quickly, to Achilles, running, to the ships of the Achaeans,
tell, if he might as quickly as possible the corpse to a ship bring safe,
naked;

Nor to you, Menelaus, Zeus-nurtured one, was the heart willing
to defend the worn-down companions, from where went away
Antilochus, and a great lack for the Pylians was made;

for as long as they run, eager to tear it apart,
but when in their midst it turns itself, trusting in its might,
back they draw away, and in fright scatter, one this way, one that.

And they, like mules, strong might having cast about them,
who drag from a mountain down a rugged footpath
either a beam or a great ship’s timber;

which even of mighty rivers the grievous streams
checks, and at once for all the current to the plain it turns,
making it stray;
